  "result": "Done! I've added the `mergeCustomers` function to handle duplicate customer merging. Here's what was implemented:\n\n**Function: `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)`**\n- Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` where the customer with `fromId` is removed and all their invoices are reassigned to `intoId`\n- Normalizes both IDs (trim & uppercase) for consistent matching\n- **Errors:**\n  - `CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND`: if either customer ID doesn't exist\n  - `SAME_CUSTOMER`: if both IDs refer to the same customer\n\n**Tests added** (6 new tests, all passing):\n1. Successful merge with invoice reassignment\n2. ID normalization during merge\n3. Error when fromId doesn't exist\n4. Error when intoId doesn't exist\n5. Error when both IDs are identical\n6. Error with normalized IDs being identical\n\nAll 12 customer tests pass \u2714",
